@startuml use-case-choreography
!include style.iuml
title ChorNMT - choreography use cases
left to right direction

actor "Authority\n(account 0)" as Authority
actor "Holder" as Holder
actor "Partner\n(account 1)" as Partner
actor "Anyone" as Anyone

rectangle "ChoreographyNMT + ChoreographyMutableAsset" {
  usecase "Mint an instance of the\nchoreography type" as UC_Mint
  usecase "Transfer the choreography\nto an eligible holder" as UC_Transfer
  usecase "Replace the Master policy\n(a new hardcoded Master)" as UC_Master
  usecase "Replace the Creator policy\n(install scenario constraints)" as UC_Creator
  usecase "Apply a BPMN delta\n(setNodes)" as UC_Nodes
  usecase "Update roles\n(setRoles)" as UC_Roles
  usecase "Link a role to a\nparticipant license" as UC_Link
  usecase "Check domain constraints\n(Creator AND Holder)" as UC_Domain
  usecase "Install a Holder policy\n(e.g. DenyAllSmartPolicy)" as UC_Holder
  usecase "Read the model\n(tokenURI)" as UC_Read
  usecase "Render the BPMN\n(off-chain)" as UC_Render
}

Authority --> UC_Mint
Authority --> UC_Master
Authority --> UC_Creator

Holder --> UC_Nodes
Holder --> UC_Roles
Holder --> UC_Holder
Holder --> UC_Transfer
UC_Link .> UC_Roles : <<extend>>
UC_Nodes ..> UC_Domain : <<include>>
UC_Roles ..> UC_Domain : <<include>>

Partner --> UC_Transfer : receives

Anyone --> UC_Read
Anyone --> UC_Render
UC_Render ..> UC_Read : <<include>>

note bottom of UC_Domain
  evaluateNodeUpdate / evaluateRoleUpdate
  of IChoreographyPolicy, asked of both
  the Creator and the Holder policy.
end note
@enduml
